                <pb facs="0874" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.105/469: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-19T17:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Your despatch No. 156 of October 12, 1933. You are authorized to amend the
                    Garde Agreement by exchange of notes. The text of the Haitian note however
                    should include the phrase “not to exceed” <pb facs="0875" n="787" xml:id="pg787"
                    /> before the word “nine” in paragraph numbered 1, if the same phrase is
                    included in the text of the Legation’s note.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
